    "title": "With Thousands of Cattle Bred… - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Codi Vallery-Mills, Cattle Business Weekly ,\n16 hours ago Thousands of miles. Thousands of cattle. Thousands of handshakes and smiles. As Anita Pepin of rural Belle Fourche, South Dakota, looks back on her career as an ABS rep and AI technician, she can’t quite put a guess on the number of miles she’s traveled, cows she’s bred, or customers’ hands she’s shaken. “It’s A LOT,” she says. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
